# Nav crawl console coverage (hard rule)

Operator defect (2026-08-19): agents claimed all-pages / comprehensive UI
coverage from hardcoded route lists, heading asserts, or chrome-only
walks while nested nav leaves were never clicked, console `TypeError`s
and `Missing string:` banners did not fail the run, blank pages after a
mid-walk deploy were counted green, and locale was assumed rather than
verified in-product. Separately, localization heal storms produced HTTP
429s that were dismissed as “test noise.” RCA:
`pim-offline-server/docs/dev/i18n-429-request-storm-rca-20260819.md`.

## The rule

> **Never claim comprehensive, all-pages, full UI, or nav crawl “works,”
> “PASS,” or “clean” unless a nav-driven Playwright (or equivalent)
> crawl expanded every left-nav menu and submenu, clicked every leaf,
> verified locale in-product, recorded served-bundle identity, and
> failed the run on product console errors, pageerrors, error
> boundaries, blank/non-rendered routes, missing-string banners / raw
> i18n keys, and 429 storms. Chrome-only nav, hardcoded route lists that
> skip nested leaves, and warning-only console collection are forbidden
> as comprehensive coverage.**

## When this rule applies

Trigger phrases (non-exhaustive): comprehensive UI test, all-pages
crawl, full admin walk, nav crawl complete, console-clean matrix,
locale walk for every shipped pack derived from US English (`en`),
“every menu tested.”

Does **not** force a full nav crawl for a narrowly scoped single-page
layout fix that explicitly scopes out comprehensive coverage (still must
not claim all-pages PASS).

## Required proof

| # | Requirement | Pass condition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | **All-sources denominator** | Crawl leaf set is the **de-duplicated union** of: SPA router (parents, index, redirects, leaves, tabbed children, gated routes), sidebar + section landings + in-app links, docs/about/legal, error/edge probes, login/pre-auth. Helper: `ui/e2e/helpers/nav-crawl-routes.mjs`. Inventory evidence: `docs/dev/evidence/nav-crawl-zh-tw-20260819/ROUTE_INVENTORY_ALL_SOURCES.md` (folder name is a **2026-08-19 incident label**, not the program — new runs use `docs/dev/evidence/nav-crawl-<YYYYMMDD>/` with per-tag matrices). **Menu-only or accordion-only lists are FAIL.** Shrinking the union vs prior inventory without an explicit exclusion note is FAIL. |
| 1 | **Nav-driven** | Every union path is visited (goto or drawer click). Accordion expand is optional when the source inventory already lists every leaf — omitting a path because an accordion was collapsed is still FAIL |
| 2 | **Locale in-product** | Header chip / `html.lang` / visible BCP-47 tag matches the intended pack for that run |
| 3 | **Served bundle** | Record disk-or-served asset identity for the run (SPA hash) |
| 4 | **Console / pageerror** | Product console errors and `pageerror` → **FAIL** (known third-party noise may filter; `TypeError`, `Missing string:`, error-boundary text may not) |
| 5 | **Render** | Route that never rendered / blank body → **FAIL**, never omitted or passed |
| 6 | **Missing strings** | Visible `Missing string:` / missing-key banner / raw key chrome → **FAIL** |
| 7 | **429 storms** | Elevated 429 counts are a **product defect** (fix client storm or name BLOCKED) — not flaky test noise |
| 8 | **Wall-clock** | A single-locale full-leaf crawl that cannot finish in a **reasonable** time (order of **~2 minutes** on a healthy unlimited lab, not hours) is itself a **defect** — usually lab rate limiting still on, or an inefficient crawl→fix→rebuild→retest loop. Slow verification is what leads to skipped verification |
| 9 | **≤10 s / page** | Each route must complete under a **hard 10 second** budget (`elapsed_ms` in the matrix). Exceeding the budget is **FAIL** with evidence — never raise the budget to green a slow page. Minutes per page is a **harness defect**. No `networkidle`, no fixed multi-second sleeps, no per-route re-auth |
| 10 | **Safe dialogs** | Where a page's primary dialogs/drawers open without mutating (no mail/SMS/rotate/PIN), open and check strings; list separately from route count |

**Locale program:** US English (`en`) is the source of truth. Every
derived pack is required at equal weight: `en-GB`, `de`, `fr`, `es`,
`zh-Hans`, `zh-TW`, and any later shipped tag. A missing key, stale
served catalog, or placeholder mismatch in **any** derived pack is the
same class of defect. A single-tag walk (including a historical zh-TW
banner incident) is not the product use case.

Canonical spec:
`pim-offline-server/ui/e2e/nav-crawl-console-embedded-live.spec.ts`
(parameterized for every shipped tag). Historical 2026-08-19 matrices
live under `docs/dev/evidence/nav-crawl-zh-tw-20260819/` — that folder
name is a dated incident label; new evidence goes to
`docs/dev/evidence/nav-crawl-<YYYYMMDD>/` with per-tag matrices inside.

## Missing-string banner = build/deploy gate failure

A visible `Missing string:` / missing-key banner in operator chrome means
an incomplete pack **already shipped**. That is not an i18n content chore
for the crawl — it is a **fail-closed build/deploy defect**.

| Gate | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Key parity (code→`en`, `en`→all tags) | `ui/scripts/assert-ui-locale-key-parity.mjs` (prebuild `--keys-only`; full shape/placeholder mode available) |
| Served pack = install artifact | `scripts/Assert-ServedUiLocalePacks.ps1` (end of `Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1`) |

Bundle hash `disk=served` proves **JS only** — it does not prove
`/locales/ui` JSON. Always run the served-pack assert after deploy.
RCA: `docs/dev/localization-fixes-lost-on-deploy-rca-20260819.md`.

## Forbidden “false green”


- Hardcoded route arrays that never expand nested drawer groups
- **MenuItems-only** or **accordion-only** denominators that omit router parents (`/access`), redirects (`/events`), messaging children, `/login`, docs/about, or 404 edge chrome
- Heading-visible / nav-label asserts without body render checks
- Collecting console errors as notes while still exiting 0
- Passing blank pages (deploy bounce, AuthBound shell, empty main)
- Assuming locale from cookie/init script without in-product verify
- Treating HTTP 429 storms as acceptable Playwright noise
- Claiming comprehensive coverage from Connect / binder / messaging
  sibling matrices alone
- “Passing” a crawl that spent hours sleeping / backing off around 429s
  instead of turning lab rate limiting off first
  ([`rate-limiting-off-for-testing.mdc`](rate-limiting-off-for-testing.mdc))
- Reporting PASS with a **smaller** route total than the last all-sources
  inventory without naming each removed path and why

## Required agent behavior

1. **Unlimited lab first** — before a crawl: confirm
   [`rate-limiting-off-for-testing.mdc`](rate-limiting-off-for-testing.mdc)
   posture (lab-dev / `REQUEST_RATE_LIMITING_ENABLED=false`, or until that
   binary is served: `ADMIN_AUTH_LOCKOUT_ENABLED=false`). Do **not** burn
   the sweep on Retry-After sleeps.
2. When claiming comprehensive / all-pages UI coverage: name the nav-crawl
   spec (or equivalent evidence) and the per-locale matrix path.
3. Fail closed on console / boundary / blank / missing-string / 429 storm.
4. Prefer SPA nav clicks after first load; never green a route that did
   not render. Batch defects from one crawl, fix the list, re-crawl once —
   do not serialize crawl→fix-one→rebuild→crawl.
5. Locale JSON: edit `locales/ui/<tag>/` on disk and reload — **no rebuild**.
   SPA behavior: Vite against the live API — **no re-embed**. Full deploy
   only when embedding is required; say *pending full deploy* otherwise.
6. Cross-link
   [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc)
   (layout proof) and
   [`session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc`](session-connect-protocol-surface.mdc)
   / [`mailpit-messaging-comprehensive-test.mdc`](mailpit-messaging-comprehensive-test.mdc)
   / [`assessment-binder-section-content.mdc`](assessment-binder-section-content.mdc)
   (sibling false-green classes).
7. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change
   set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** “All admin pages PASS” from a static `ROUTES[]` goto loop
in English only; nested PAM / Configuration leaves never opened;
`i18n: missing string` console lines ignored; 40× 429 during the walk
called “rate-limit flake.”

**Fix:** Run `nav-crawl-console-embedded-live.spec.ts` for **every**
shipped tag derived from `en` (or `node e2e/run-nav-crawl-all-locales.mjs`);
fail on console / missing-string / blank / 429 storm; fix packs and
client heal; record per-tag matrices under
`docs/dev/evidence/nav-crawl-<YYYYMMDD>/`. A 2026-08-19 zh-TW banner
is one worked example of the same defect class — not the crawl’s
canonical locale.

